The strategy of focusing on easily obtainable biofluids and evaluating markers directly linked to ALS pathogenesis stands as a cornerstone for the effective development of biomarkers. The occurrence of ferroptosis in motor neurons is increasingly acknowledged as a vital aspect of ALS with markers like lipid and iron accumulation signaling this specific type of programmed cell death [
