Analyzing both the MCP-1 and FOXP3 mRNA, distinct effects were observed within the PP population. Among other findings, a significant change over time was solely detected in the PP population for actin-NT with no other notable effects identified for other biomarkers in the studied populations. To detect a 44% decrease in the progression rate of PPIA with 80% power, a total of 142 patients was deemed necessary. Likewise, the study aimed to discern a 43% reduction in ALSFRS-R progression over 24 weeks and a 25% absolute decrease in patients becoming non-self-sufficient at the 24-week mark [
